<title>USA: Fannie Mae sets $900 mln REMIC 1997-39.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae sets $900 mln REMIC 1997-39.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae said it issued $900 million of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities via Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p>REMIC trust 1997-39 is backed by 30-year, 8.5 percent mortgage-backed securities and Ginnie Mae 30-year 7.5 percent certificates, the agency said.</p>
<p>The issue priced on April 24 and has a settlement date of May 30, Fannie Mae said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
